<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African January trade data now due next Tuesday.</title>
<headline>S.African January trade data now due next Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>January trade statistics had been scheduled for release on February 25, a South African Revenue Services spokesman said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The data had originally been expected to be released this week.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast an 817 million rand surplus for the month compared with a 2.04 billion rand surplus in December last year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
